  "description": "meme-id: fuck_banks_fuck_indians_too; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image uses a historical photograph of a stern-looking man in military uniform (likely General Custer) with the text 'fuck banks' and 'fuck indians too'. This juxtaposition is intended to convey a message of extreme anger and contempt toward both financial institutions and Native American peoples. The meme leverages the historical association of General Custer with the Battle of Little Bighorn, where he was defeated by Native American forces, to imply that the depicted figure represents a violent, aggressive, and ultimately destructive force. The intent is to express a visceral, hateful sentiment toward both banks (as symbols of systemic exploitation and greed) and Native Americans (as a historically oppressed group). The use of the word 'fuck' and the direct targeting of two distinct groups — one representing modern economic power structures and the other representing a marginalized indigenous population — indicates a hateful intent. The meme does not target individuals but rather groups based on their identity and historical context, fitting the definition of hateful content as it attacks specific communities based on protected characteristics (race/ethnicity and economic institution).",
